WEBVTT

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.410
Mon Chaton.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.290
Listen to me well.

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:23.210
You must never let anyone
take your true name.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.470
It is the formula that
gives shape to who you are.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.600
That is to say...

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.680
...it is your very life.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:47.110
I want you to give me your true name.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:48.610
<i>Non!</i>

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.160
What are you doing, Noé?

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.290
Did you twist your ankle dancing?

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.330
Who are you?

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.420
So, you're from Charlatan?

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.880
There's blood on your neck. Are you hurt?

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.220
I don't kiss and tell.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:25.230
Stay away from Master Luca!

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:37.530
THE 
CASE
 STUDY 
OF 
VANITAS

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:45.290
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.670
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:54.260
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:59.510
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:07.020
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:15.610
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:24.580
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.460
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:34.130
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.720
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.480
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:52.320
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.280
You said you're from Charlatan.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.750
What is it you want?

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.960
Was this pandemonium your doing?

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.510
How delightful.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.090
How very delightful!

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:25.350
Enough, Naenia.
We've already been here too long.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.850
The Queen's Fangs
will soon get wind of this.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.520
Tsk, how disappointing.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.530
That voice is the same as before.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.370
Noé.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:52.290
I've taken a liking to you.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:57.840
When next we meet,
I want you to give me your true name.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.090
Wait! What do you want?!

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.390
Why are you creating curse-bearers?

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:03.890
And Louis! Why did you--?

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.890
Bye-bye, Noé.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.770
Get back here!

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:09.980
After them!

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.980
Yes, Master Luca!

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:14.940
Wait for me!

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.740
Noé!

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.740
I'm so glad I found you!

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.620
It's bedlam in the great hall.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.530
Are you all right?

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.920
Domi.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.670
Noé?

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:37.840
Get a hold of yourself!
There are curse-bearers in the great hall!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.090
They all appeared at once!

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:42.590
And those who blacked out

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.140
are being driven mad by
the curse-bearers' voices.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:50.100
That is the malnomen Dissonance,
the Beastly Orchestra.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:59.240
This rare malnomen occurs when those
afflicted with maladies gather together.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:04.620
The voice they make creates a dissonance
that drives all around them mad.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.000
And you are the one
who can save them, human?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.040
I'll see what I can do.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.840
Very well.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:23.970
Then I will protect you.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:27.510
Curse-bearer heads will
roll if we don't act now.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:30.350
Quickly!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.770
That's right.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:34.020
Things are different now.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.730
The power Vanitas wields--

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.030
it can save them!

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.280
There! Your first patient!

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.890
Who the devil are they?

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.470
The Clan of the Blue Moon!

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:15.350
Was it you who turned
them into curse-bearers?

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.810
Kill him.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.770
Kill him.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:18.770
Kill him!

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:19.900
Kill him!

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.900
Kill that human!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.280
Vanitas, I must thank you.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.700
What's with you?

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.740
Nothing. It's just...

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.700
I wished to say that.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.630
Noé, you're a bit clueless.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.720
This is bad! Get out of here!

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:47.720
Domi!

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.890
From what I saw,
I'd say there's one curse-bearer left.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:51.600
But--

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.310
Now, go!

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.230
If you don't...

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:02.610
Domi, my dear!

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:08.110
Whatever are you doing with that mortal?

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:12.240
You're looking well, Sister Veronica.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Me, clueless?

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.670
About what?

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:22.800
And you are the one
who can save them, human?

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.510
I'll see what I can do.

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:28.340
Vanitas...

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:36.520
Catherine, stop.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.740
She's...

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:53.620
It's too late for this one.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:08:00.500
There's no going back once
the flesh is as corrupted as this.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:05.670
Kill... me. Kill... me.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:12.800
Kill me before I murder
my little sister, too.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.350
Vanitas.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:19.140
Please, wait. Vanitas!

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.480
Stay out of the way, Noé.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.120
I see.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.330
No.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.290
So that's your true name.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.790
Don't!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.420
It suits you well.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.080
No!

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.300
Why?!

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.930
Huh? What's got your knickers in a knot?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.270
I've said it from the start, haven't I?

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:02.480
It matters not what you people want!

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.820
I <i>will </i>save the vampires.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.360
I will do as I please.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.820
I will use the methods I choose.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.950
It matters not what you people want!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:20.000
I <i>will </i>save the vampires.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:27.250
Is this... salvation?

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.510
Kill... me.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.930
Kill me. Kill me, Noé.

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.730
I don't understand.

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.690
Vanitas.

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:46.610
What is salvation?!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.900
Tell me. What is salvation?!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.150
As if I'd know.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.410
Make of it what you will.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:03.370
I found you!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.340
Marquis Machina! Hurry!

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.550
Stop my sister before it's too late!

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.600
Oh, the stench, the stench, the stench!

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.980
It reeks of man. The stink of humans!

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:27.810
There is truly nothing worse.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.860
That mask is obstructing her sight,

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.530
yet she can still
rewrite formulas like this?!

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:39.660
Those <i>are </i>some incredible eyes you have,

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.910
Veronica de Sade, the Queen's Fangs.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:47.830
Mine is not a name that ought to
roll off your tongue so lightly, mortal.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.420
Yikes.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.640
First, I shall freeze you.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.390
And after that? Let me think.

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:00.810
Vanitas!

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:06.100
Curses! That single attack
has rendered my body...

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:11.070
Now, before the eyes of
dear little Domi, who tried to stop me,

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:15.360
I shall smash you into tiny icy bits.

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:38.510
That's enough, Veronica.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:40.800
The Queen's Fangs, of all people,

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:45.020
should not make such an
unbecoming display of power.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:49.690
Lord Ruthven.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:53.570
Ruthven? Where have
I heard that name before?

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:56.440
You have arrived quite late.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:00.410
Indeed. My carriage was
attacked by assailants unknown.

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:04.330
And it took longer than
expected to find another.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:08.580
Now then, what has transpired here?

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:13.840
That mortal man is of
the Clan of the Blue Moon.

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:17.590
His arm bears the clan's foul mark.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:21.850
Several curse-bearers appeared
soon after he revealed it.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:26.560
I believe he used <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>
to spread the Curse of the Blue Moon.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.270
No!

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:32.480
Is what I just heard true?

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:38.450
Was it you who turned her into ashes?

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:45.700
That's right. It was I who slew the girl.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.760
No!

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:02.590
Don't you lay a finger on him!

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:06.350
I don't know who you are,
but you better listen!

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:10.230
I was in the middle of speaking with him.

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:12.350
Then you people barged in!

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.230
Who do you think you are?!

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:17.730
Don't draw your own conclusions
when you haven't a clue!

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.950
I will not let you pin the blame on him!

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.120
Wait a minute.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.370
Did I do the same?

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:43.010
My apologies. It is as you say, young man.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:46.970
It was I who lacked for manners.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:49.100
I am Ruthven.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:54.270
I serve Her Majesty, the Queen,
as a member of the Senate.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:57.070
The Senate?

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.570
Lord Uncle!

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:03.150
Lucius. I'm delighted
to see you're unharmed.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:07.740
It was I who was worried about you!
I feared something had happened.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.790
Luca?

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:10.370
Uncle?

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.830
Steady there.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.090
Don't!

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:21.590
Have no fear. I merely
wish to melt the ice.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:34.690
Lord Uncle, what will you do with them?

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:40.030
I shall take the two
of them under my wing.

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:42.190
And as you are no doubt aware,

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:47.570
all who dare do harm to guests
of mine know the peril it brings.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:53.040
For such an act shall be deemed
as an attack upon my person.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.090
Vanitas.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:08.470
I owe you...

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.010
...an apology.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:18.230
An apology? Whatever for?

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:21.480
Teacher?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:30.330
I tried to force my hopes
and ideals upon him.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:36.960
He never claimed anything
other than what he said,

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:43.510
but my expectations grew of my own accord,
leading to feelings of betrayal.

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:47.630
I am so callow, Teacher.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.390
And?

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:55.480
He did not live up to your hopes,
so you couldn't stand being around him?

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.190
Mon Chaton.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:05.240
When I told you to assess the
true nature of <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>,

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:10.700
it was not to reveal whether
it was a threat to us.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.330
Huh?

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:20.960
I wish for you to meet those
whose paths cross the book.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:23.800
You must experience their stories.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:31.970
Upon doing so, how shall you
characterize the book on your own terms?

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:35.890
<i>That </i>is what I wish to know.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:30.610
You really do like heights.

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:35.410
Can I ask what happened after that?

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:38.290
Nothing that interesting.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:42.920
Lord Ruthven diffused the situation
and dispersed the crowd.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:47.340
We're now ostensibly
His Lordship's "guests."

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:50.340
So that was him in the room I was in?

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.010
Yes.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.010
Hey.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:17:59.140
What's the matter?

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.480
What do you mean?

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:02.100
You're mad about something.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.140
Huh?

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.900
If not, then you're pouting.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:06.730
Don't be stupid.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:13.360
I know you wish to say something to me.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:14.200
Nope.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.280
Well, I do.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:21.830
You said what you are doing
is an act of vengeance.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:22.790
And?

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:25.540
What did you mean by that?
I wish to know--

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:27.670
That was a lie.

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:28.630
It was?

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:29.840
That's right.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:35.800
I thought no vampire would pay me
heed unless I said something like that.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.760
You fell for it, didn't you? Idiot!

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:40.180
You're lying.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:43.850
You're lying about saying you lied.

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:47.060
Whether you seek this or not,

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.570
I <i>will </i>save you vampires!

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:51.610
That very deed

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:56.910
will be my ultimate act of
vengeance against Vanitas!

00:18:56.910 --> 00:19:00.370
When you said that, I finally understood.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.500
That's why you have that look at times.

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:07.830
It's as if you have given up on something.

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:17.840
Stop trying to paint me
with your silly assumptions.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.060
Enough, you wet blanket!

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:23.180
I can't deal with
simple-minded fools like you!

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:26.650
I want nothing further to do with you!

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:28.270
So you had better--

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.690
What?

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:33.820
I don't even know
why I'm listening to you.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:41.330
Perhaps you have got the wrong idea,
but I really don't like you.

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:44.830
As such, I have no intention
of following your orders

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.250
or assisting you in any way.

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:50.540
And I'm saying you don't need to!

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:12.110
Just when I thought he was angry,
he starts sulking.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:14.440
How interesting.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:18.820
I really don't understand
what he is thinking.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:21.320
He speaks of salvation.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:25.120
What does that really mean?

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:27.120
I must know.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.000
I must.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:37.260
However, I do find you intriguing, human.

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:42.510
I wish to see your labors
and witness their outcome.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.520
And should you refuse me,

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:59.150
I shall still do as I please,
your will notwithstanding.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:06.790
I've decided to remain
by your side, Vanitas.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:19.300
I couldn't care less.

00:21:24.890 --> 00:21:30.310
The color of the rising sun that morning
remains quite vivid in my mind.

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:36.690
But memories of the beginning
readily evoke memories of the end.

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:42.740
Memories of what slipped from my grasp.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:45.990
The people I could not protect.

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:49.580
The day I could not grab your hand.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:52.080
These are my regrets.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.880
Oh, and...

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.340
Vanitas, I'm sorry.

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:05.640
For what?

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:09.520
Nothing. I simply wished to say that.

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:17.060
Questions

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:52.070
Love
